      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Leafs",
        "body": "The Leafs have spent the week narrowing the noise - and the roster - with September's dress rehearsal finally giving way to real decisions. <strong>Steven Lorentz cleared waivers after Toronto's final preseason cutdown, a small but telling win for a team trimming toward opening night.</strong> The exhibition record ended at 2-2, with two wins over Ottawa after two losses to Montreal, but the only score that matters now is the one on Tuesday in the opener against the Canadiens. That's where the new faces and the new goalie mix stop being theory and start being judged. Lorentz's survival matters because depth wins autumn jobs. <strong>Next comes Montreal on Tuesday, and the first test of whether this reshaped group can look like a contender instead of a work in progress.</strong>",
        "updated": "Updated September 27, 2026"
      },
