        "body": "The last day of a lost season arrives with little romance and a lot of housekeeping - one more turn at the yard, one more chance to see what still matters. <strong>The Blue Jays were beaten 5-1 by the Reds on Sept. 26</strong>, leaving them 78-83 and 5th in the AL East, and they'll close it out Sunday afternoon against Cincinnati at Rogers Centre. Max Scherzer gets the ball in the finale, and the old right-hander says the decision on 2027 can wait until the winter; that's the headline, because the rest of this roster is already being sorted. The young arms and bench bats will get their look now, the last auditions before the winter lists begin. <strong>What matters next is simple: watch Scherzer's farewell, then watch which kids earn a real place in the offseason plans.</strong>",
